{
  "_about": "Music registry, one entry per track (lane B4 fills it). Files live in assets/audio/86/ (personal use only: git-ignored, and its .gdignore keeps Godot from importing or exporting them), so \"path\" is relative to the project folder (an absolute or ~ path also works) and a missing file is skipped quietly. Entry shape: {\"title\": \"...\", \"path\": \"assets/audio/86/...\", \"language\": \"en\" | \"ja\" | \"none\", \"kind\": \"opening\" | \"ending\" | \"score\", \"loop\": true, \"loop_start_s\": 0, \"loop_end_s\": null, \"use\": [\"menu\", \"combat\", \"explore\"]}. Set \"free\" (Relay 95): royalty-free tracks that ship with the game in assets/audio/free/ (tracked, imported, exported; licence and credit per entry, listed in assets/SOURCES.md). They are the Soundtrack of a copy without the 86 music and no music folder, and hidden otherwise. tools/audio/fetch_music.py keeps them.",
